    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today's slate with a high-ceiling lineup led by **Christian Yelich** (74.33) and **Trea Turner** (71.71). **Christian Yelich** is the standout play; he benefits from a favorable matchup against Lowder, whose 4.93 xERA suggests a prime environment for production, coupled with a massive 13% boost from his platoon advantage. Similarly, **Trea Turner** remains an essential start despite a slight drag from an elite-armed catcher; the combination of a leadoff spot and a wind-aided atmosphere in his matchup against Chandler provides the leverage needed to capitalize on stolen base opportunities, which remain our primary scarcity target. **Kyle Schwarber** (69.89) and **Junior Caminero** (69.59) round out our top-tier hitters, with both players gaining significant value from favorable wind conditions that could turn fly balls into crucial home runs.\n\nWe are keeping a close eye on **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (67.96) and **Chase Meidroth** (65.95). **Pete Crow-Armstrong** carries risk due to a dynamic platoon disadvantage against the lefty Sears, but his leadoff positioning and wind assistance maintain his efficiency above our 60-point threshold. The bench decision for **Carson Benge** (52.97) was the most difficult, as he narrowly missed the cut; ultimately, the optimizer penalized his start against a high-tier arm in Gausman, favoring the higher-floor efficiency of our active starters. While **Jacob Gonzalez** (57.55) and **Caleb Durbin** (54.79) reside in the lower end of our starting group, their strong matchup against the weak rotation of Gibson and Cavalli keeps them viable. We have successfully avoided falling below our floor with **Dillon Dingler** (36.91), who has been benched to preserve game caps and avoid a negative production outcome against tough pitching.",
